				3
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 3 core submodules for diagnostics enhancement and build refresh\n\nPerform targeted updates to the extension host pipeline and service layer to improve runtime observability and ensure build consistency.\n\n**Cocoon**: Regenerate TypeScript compilation outputs and update the `RouteManifest` timestamp to reflect the current build cycle, ensuring the extension host sidecar and gRPC services are synchronized with the latest source modifications.\n\n**Output**: Enhance the `RuntimeDiagnosticsInner` transform plugin to perform rigorous validation of the `acquireVsCodeApi` interface. Explicitly invoke the function at the 4-second mark to inspect method signatures (`postMessage`, `getState`, `setState`) and report execution results via the `VSCODE_API_TEST` event, addressing potential structural incompleteness in WKWebView environments.\n\n**Wind**: Refresh auto-generated command and service catalogs to align with the latest upstream VS Code workbench definitions, updating version constants and total counts for 546 commands and 490 services.\n\nThese changes ensure robust extension host connectivity diagnostics and consistent service layer contracts across the multi-process architecture.",
			"SHA": "416354fb31aed83b73e5022e2fe53f923b75c1fe"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-16T00:03:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡟⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				9
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 9 submodules for webview configuration and documentation standardization\n\nPerform a mass update of core Land Editor submodules to resolve critical webview rendering issues and standardize architectural documentation across the ecosystem.\n\n**Cocoon**: Fix `CreateWebviewViewBuilder` to forward user-defined webview options to the Mountain backend via gRPC, ensuring native webviews respect extension capabilities (e.g., script execution). Standardize trace logging newlines to prevent stream corruption.\n\n**Output**: Refine the `Logging` transform plugin to use regex-based insertion for Content Security Policy font fallbacks and enforce mandatory `_vscodeApiScript` injection regardless of the `allowScripts` flag. This restores functionality for extensions like Roo Code and fixes KaTeX/Codicons rendering in WKWebView.\n\n**Common, Grove, Mountain, Sky, Vine, Wind, Worker**: Align `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` files by normalizing whitespace characters (removing non-breaking spaces, narrow spaces, and em spaces) between section titles and emojis. This ensures consistent visual hierarchy and rendering across all Markdown viewers and GitHub interfaces.\n\nThese updates ensure reliable extension host configuration, robust webview initialization, and a unified technical reference for the multi-process architecture.",
			"SHA": "6b5c159affad677b0a383fe2ebdb62fc51d6fe30"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T23:37:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⡟⠀⠀",
				26,
				14
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 14 submodules for documentation standardization and webview stability\n\nPerform a mass update of all core Land Editor submodules to align documentation and runtime behavior. Most components (Air, Common, Echo, Grove, Mist, Mountain, Rest, SideCar, Sky, Vine, Wind, Worker) refine `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` with section emojis, bulleted lists, and absolute GitHub URLs for cross-referencing.\n\n**Cocoon**: Patch `Webview/Implementation.ts` to append a wildcard `font-src *` fallback to the Content Security Policy, resolving font loading failures in WKWebView where legacy protocol schemes are rejected.\n\n**Output**: Extend the `Logging` transform plugin to force injection of the `_vscodeApiScript` regardless of the `allowScripts` flag and ensure the CSP includes the font wildcard. This restores functionality for extensions like Roo Code and fixes custom font rendering.\n\n**Sky**: Refactor `Bridge.ts` to use bracket notation for dynamic `Wire` DTO property access, enforcing strict TypeScript compliance.\n\nThese updates ensure consistent technical documentation across the ecosystem and resolve critical webview rendering and API initialization issues on macOS.",
			"SHA": "c026dc1f1887ac086314e85b208affe799427d4b"
		}
